## FEATURE (context)
A one-shot button "Draw 3D Guide" in GuideBar. When active, the NEXT stroke is drawn normally and ALSO creates a
transparent guide plane through that stroke, perpendicular to the surface it was drawn on.
Plane normal = normalize(chord x surfaceNormal), chord = last point - first point. Origin = midpoint of chord.
(Vertical line on default XY plane -> plane YZ. Horizontal line -> ground plane XZ.)
Later strokes snap to the nearest guide plane (or base sphere/cube) under the pointer, and stay LOCKED to the
surface where the stroke started. Creating the guide is part of the same undo step as the stroke.

